{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCites are on origin/main 083620b0. `src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py` is a whole-file re-export of `rebar._ids` (its docstring `:8` says \"every existing importer is unchanged\"). `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py:18-31` re-exports 7 names from `_processors_identity`/`_processors_status` marked `# noqa: F401 (re-exported for back-compat)`: `_rederive_keyring_keys`, `process_key_event`, `process_signature`, `_fold_claimed_session`, `_fold_close_metadata`, `_fold_plan_review_phase`, `process_status`. ADR 0111 (`docs/adr/0111-no-internal-only-compatibility-shims.md:40-57`) forbids internal-only shims and requires atomic migration of \"source, test, string, dynamic import, and monkeypatch\" targets. This story touches import and prose lines only, every file named below or in the first comment; landing it first means every other epic rebases over one-line import diffs.\n\n## Approach\nOne change: rewrite every importer to the canonical module, delete the resolver shim and the seven re-export lines, fix the monkeypatch string and the one shim-asserting test. Population found by Serena `find_referencing_symbols` on `resolve_ticket_id` plus `git grep` for the module strings (both required by AGENTS.md); the lists below are the whole population, not samples.\n\nResolver: the 58 plain `from rebar._engine_support.resolver import X` sites in 43 files (1 script line, 42 `src/` lines across 31 modules, 15 test lines; every file and line is itemised in this ticket's first comment) become `from rebar._ids import X`. Module-object form: `tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py:46` and `tests/unit/test_close_precheck_duplicate_link_c8fd.py:59` (`from rebar._engine_support import resolver as _resolver` becomes `from rebar import _ids as _resolver`) and `tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py:397`, which has NO alias (`from rebar._engine_support import resolver`, consumed as the bare name `resolver` by `monkeypatch.setattr(resolver, \"build_resolver_scan_index\", ...)` at `:409`) and becomes `from rebar import _ids as resolver`. Attribute form `rebar._engine_support.resolver.resolve_ticket_id(...)` becomes `rebar._ids.resolve_ticket_id(...)` at `tests/unit/{test_compact_sweep_perf.py:75, test_compact_trigger.py:70, test_completion_sidecar_lock_loss_ab54.py:99, test_relocated_store_repo_root.py:240}`. Monkeypatch string `tests/unit/test_completion_sidecar_material_balding.py:228` becomes `\"rebar._ids.resolve_ticket_dir_name\"` (valid because every consumer imports in-body from `rebar._ids`). Prose at `docs/bash-migration.md:168`, `src/rebar/_alias.py:4,36`, `src/rebar/_ids.py:23`, `tests/scripts/reducer/test_ticket_alias_backfill.py:7,119` says `rebar._ids`. Delete `src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py`.\n\nProcessors: in `_processors.py` delete lines 21, 23, 24, 27-30 (the seven `noqa` re-exports); keep `_bootstrap_genesis_keyring`, `_fold_author_attribution`, `attestation_kind`, which the module body uses at `:81,155,213,344,609,627`. Every importer of the seven names goes through the shim today and is rewritten: `src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py:19-38` currently imports `process_key_event` (`:27`), `process_signature` (`:30`) and `process_status` (`:32`) from `._processors`; split that list so those two come from `._processors_identity` and `process_status` from `._processors_status`, the other sixteen `process_*` names staying on `._processors`. Tests: `tests/unit/test_attestations_reducer.py:13-18` (`process_signature` from `rebar.reducer._processors_identity`, `process_status` from `rebar.reducer._processors_status`; `attestation_kind` and `process_snapshot` stay on `_processors`), `tests/unit/test_claimed_session.py:20`, `tests/unit/test_harness_provenance.py:20`, `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_happy.py:6`, `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py:10` (`process_status` from `_processors_status`; `process_snapshot` stays), `tests/unit/test_legacy_signature_mirror_drop.py:15` and `tests/unit/test_signing.py:316,332` (`process_signature` from `_processors_identity`). `tests/unit/test_processors_status_split.py:18-34` asserts the four `_processors_status` names resolve through the shim, so it cannot survive: move `test_status_fold_replay_equivalence` and `_apply_status` into `tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py`, rewriting the helper body from `processors_status.process_status(...)` to the bare `process_status(...)` that module imports, and `git rm` the file (the test-suite epic's seam story skips it once gone). `_rederive_keyring_keys` and the three `_fold_*` names have no other external importer (`tests/unit/test_administrative_close_dispositions.py:369-384` already calls `_processors_status._fold_close_metadata` directly). Importers of names `_processors.py` defines itself (`attestation_kind`, `process_create`, `process_snapshot`, `process_tag_delta`, `_file_impact_scope`, `_KNOWN_TICKET_STATUSES`) are untouched.\n\n## Scope\nExactly the files above: `src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py` (deleted), `tests/unit/test_processors_status_split.py` (deleted), `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`, `src/rebar/reducer/_replay.py`, the listed `src/rebar/_commands/*.py`, `src/rebar/_engine_support/*.py`, `src/rebar/llm/**/*.py`, `src/rebar/{_lib_writes.py,signing.py,audit/read.py,metrics/blame.py,review_bot/artifact_emit.py,_alias.py,_ids.py}`, `scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py`, `docs/bash-migration.md`, and the listed `tests/**` files. Out of scope: any behaviour change, any new name, and the bodies of the canonical modules `rebar._ids`, `_processors_identity` and `_processors_status`.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy: `git grep -n -E '_engine_support\\.resolver|_engine_support import resolver' -- src tests scripts` returns nothing; `python -c \"import rebar._engine_support.resolver\"` raises `ModuleNotFoundError`.\n- Edge: `pytest tests/unit/test_completion_sidecar_material_balding.py tests/unit/commands/test_replacement_walker.py tests/unit/test_close_precheck_duplicate_link_c8fd.py tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py -q` green (monkeypatch retargeting, the un-aliased module object, and the moved fold test).\n- `ruff check src tests scripts` reports no F401 in `_processors.py`; `pytest tests/unit/test_attestations_reducer.py tests/unit/test_signing.py tests/unit/test_legacy_signature_mirror_drop.py -q` green; `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py` is deleted and `git grep -n -E '_engine_support\\.resolver|_engine_support import resolver' -- src tests scripts` prints nothing.\n- [ ] `_processors.py` contains no `re-exported for back-compat` line, and `git grep -n -E '^\\s*from rebar\\.reducer\\._processors import|^\\s*from \\._processors import' -- src tests` followed by a check of each hit's imported names shows none of `process_status`, `process_signature`, `process_key_event`, `_rederive_keyring_keys`, `_fold_claimed_session`, `_fold_close_metadata`, `_fold_plan_review_phase` (a script over the AST of each hit records the result on this ticket).\n- [ ] `tests/unit/test_processors_status_split.py` is gone and `pytest --collect-only -q tests/unit/test_plan_review_phase_reducer.py::test_status_fold_replay_equivalence` collects one node.\n- [ ] `python -c \"import rebar._engine_support.resolver\"` raises `ModuleNotFoundError` and the edge-test set above is green under `pytest`.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788814488306277929,"uuid":"e002b837-3299-47de-9aa9-d81c56e642c4"}